Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sun May 3 11:30:08 2026 +1000

    Drop redundant rabbitmq-erlang PPA on Debian.
    
    The kolla-toolbox and rabbitmq images on Debian enable the
    rabbitmq-erlang PPA hosted on Launchpad
    (ppa.launchpadcontent.net) to obtain Erlang 27. Debian Trixie now
    ships erlang-base 1:27.3.4.1+dfsg-1+deb13u1 in the base archive,
    which already satisfies the ``erlang* version 1:27.*`` pin in
    apt_preferences_rabbitmq.debian. The PPA is therefore no longer
    needed for Debian builds and adds an avoidable dependency on
    Canonical infrastructure -- recent Launchpad outages have
    repeatedly broken Debian image builds at the apt-get update step.
    
    The Ubuntu builds still need the PPA because Ubuntu Noble only
    ships Erlang 25, and the RPM-based Rocky and CentOS builds still
    need the rpm-side erlang repo, so this change special-cases only
    Debian: when base_distro == 'debian' we enable just the rabbitmq
    repo, otherwise the original ['erlang', 'rabbitmq'] call is kept
    intact. The now-unused debian.erlang entry is removed from
    kolla/template/repos.yaml. The rabbitmq-server package continues
    to come from deb1.rabbitmq.com on both Debian and Ubuntu.
    
    Prompt: Is the use of the failing launchpad Erlang PPA still needed,
    or have the operating system packages caught up and are now
    sufficiently modern?
    
