@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+---
+upgrade:
+  - |
+    The ``kolla-toolbox`` and ``rabbitmq`` images on Debian no longer
+    enable the ``rabbitmq-erlang`` PPA hosted on Launchpad
+    (``ppa.launchpadcontent.net``). Debian Trixie now ships
+    ``erlang-base`` 1:27.x in its base archive, which already satisfies
+    the ``erlang* version 1:27.*`` pin in
+    ``apt_preferences_rabbitmq.debian``. The ``rabbitmq-server`` package
+    continues to come from ``deb1.rabbitmq.com``.
+
+    The Ubuntu and RPM (Rocky/CentOS) image builds are unchanged:
+    Ubuntu still enables the rabbitmq-erlang PPA because Noble only
+    ships Erlang 25, and Rocky/CentOS still enable the rpm-side
+    rabbitmq-erlang repo as before.
+
+    Removing this dependency makes the Debian image build resilient to
+    Launchpad outages, which have previously broken CI at the
+    ``apt-get update`` step.
